Robust outexpanders are the directed version of robust expanders.,
"Let ν, τ > 0 and D be a directed graph on n vertices.",
"The ν-robust outneighbourhood RN + ν,D(S) of a set S ⊆V (D) in D consists of all the vertices of D which have at least νn inneighbours in S. We say that D is a robust (ν, τ)-outexpander if |RN + ν,D(S)| ≥|S| + νn for each S ⊆V (D) satisfying τn ≤|S| ≤(1 −τ)n. We call a digraph D on n vertices (δ, f)-almost regular if all vertices of D have in- and outdegree (1 ± f)δn.",
