Bipartite graphs.,
"Of particular interest are perfect matchings in (balanced) bipartite graphs, but bipartite graphs are not robust expanders as the neighbourhood of one of the partition classes is only at most as large as the class itself.",
"However, the notion of robust expanders can be adapted to bipartite graphs.",
"Let G be a bipartite graph with vertex partition (A, B) and |A| = |B| = n. We say that G is a bipartite robust (ν, τ)-expander if |RNν,G(S)| ≥|S| + νn for each S ⊆A satisfying τn ≤|S| ≤(1 −τ)n. The following is an analogue of Theorems 1.1, 1.2, and 3.1 for bipartite graphs.",
This then also includes an approximation for the number of derangements.,
Theorem 3.3.,
