"Note also that the necessity of testing the admissibility condition over all sub-histograms of f has a clear combinatorial interpretation: If cliques with a given histogram typically appear, then for each given sub-histogram cliques with that sub-histogram must appear (just because a subset of a clique again induces a clique).",
"Now, after all the arguing why (7) should seem wrong, let us explain why it is actually all right.",
