"If κ and κ′ are two kernels on the same vertex space with κ ≤κ′, then GV(n, κ) and GV(n, κ′) are random graphs on the same vertex set, and there is a natural coupling between them in which GV(n, κ) is always a subgraph of GV(n, κ′), i.e., a coupling with G(n, κ) ⊆G(n, κ′).",
