"Each existing vertex produces new, initially isolated, vertices according to a Pois- son process with intensity γ.",
"As soon as there are at least two vertices, each vertex sends out edges according to another Poisson process with intensity λ; the other endpoint is chosen uniformly among all other existing vertices.",
"(Multiple edges are allowed, but this makes little diﬀerence.)",
"Vertices live for ever, but edges die with intensity δ, i.e., the lifetime of an edge has an exponential distribution with mean 1/δ.",
