The notations K or C are used to denote a universal constant whose exact value may change from line to line.,
Main result Let us first define the centrosymmetric matrix.,
Definition 3.1 (Centrosymmetric Matrix).,
A random Centrosymmetric matrix is a random matrix which is symmetric about its center.,
"Formally, let M = [mi,j]n×n be a random matrix, where mij are i.i.d.",
"random variables subject to the following constraint mi,j = mn−i+1,n−j+1 for i, j ∈{1, .",
Then M is called a random centrosymmetric matrix.,
Definition 3.2 (Poincar´e inequality).,
"A complex random variable ζ is said to satisfy the Poincar´e inequality with a positive constant α if for any differentiable function g : C →C, we have Var(g(ζ)) ≤ 1 αE[|g′(ζ)|2].",
