Consider 1 2 < α < 1 and ν > 0.,
"Suppose s, t are vertices added to C := Cα,ν(n) at points with radial coordinates rs, rt, respectively.",
"If the degrees of s and t are d(s) and d(t), respectively, and d(s), d(t) ⩾1, then the following holds: (i) If (1 −1 2α)R < rs, rt ⩽R − ln(R/ν) 2(α−1/2)(1−α) −Θ(1), then a.a.s., Es( τs,t ) = O  n ·  1 d(s)4α(1−α) + 1 d(t)4α(1−α)  .",
