"Similarly, for u, v ∈V we let Eu( τv ), where τv := inf{t ⩾0 | Xt = v}, be the hitting time of v from u.",
"We shall use π to denote the stationary distribution of a simple random walk on a connected graph G, given by π(v) := d(v) 2|E| for v ∈V .",
"Let thit(G) := max u,v∈V EG u ( τv ) , and t⊙(G) := X u,v∈V (G) EG u ( τv ) π(u)π(v), denote the maximum hitting time and the target time, respectively.",
We deﬁne each of these times to be 0 if G is either the empty graph or consists of just a single vertex.,
