"The latter ﬂow will also be useful later on when we consider local parameters of simple random walks in G. The term fs,H(s) will be a ({s}, V ∩H(s))-ﬂow that equally distributes the unit of ﬂow that is injected in s among all vertices in the half-tile H(s) to which s belongs.",
"Similarly, the term fH(t),t will be a balanced (V ∩H(t), {t})-ﬂow that sends towards t all the ﬂow at vertices in the half-tile H(t) to which t belongs.",
