"The term f ′ Hs,Ht will be deﬁned so that it determines a balanced ﬂow from Hs to H′ s. The underlying idea in specifying f ′ Hs,Ht consists in pushing the ﬂow from vertices in H := Hs to vertices in its twin half-tile H′, so that all vertices in the tile T := H ∪H′ end up with the same amount of ﬂow.",
"Subsequently, ﬂow is pushed through the oriented edges from vertices in T to vertices in the parent half-tile of T, so all edges involved carry exactly the same amount of ﬂow, and then repeating the process but taking H as the parent half-tile of T, and so on and so forth until H equals H′ s. Formally, we deﬁne f ′ Hs,Ht : ⃗E(G) →R so that if H ̸= H′ s and T is the tile that contains H (thus, T \ H is the twin of H), then (12) f ′ Hs,Ht( ⃗uv) := 1 |V ∩T| · 1 |V ∩H| for all u ∈V ∩H and v ∈V ∩(T \ H).",
