"Cover Time and Maximum Hitting Time In this section, we ﬁrst determine the asymptotic behavior of the cover time of the giant component of the HRG.",
"To do so, we rely on several intermediate structural results concerning HRGs that were established in the previous section.",
"However, the arguments developed here are not ﬂow based.",
"In particular, the ones concerning commute times rely on extensions of Matthew’s Bound, a classical and useful method for bounding cover times.",
"This result is then complemented, by the determination of the maximum hitting time also for the giant.",
"As in the previous sections, we restrict our discussion exclusively to the parameter range where 1 2 < α < 1.",
Upper Bounds on Hitting and Cover times.,
"As mentioned above, to determine the cover time of the center component of the HRG we rely on Matthew’s bound (stated below) and one of its extensions (mentioned later).",
The bound and its extensions relate the cover time of a graph with its minimum and maximum hitting times.,
