"We say that a subgraph P of a graph G is a dangling path if P is a path in G and there is a single edge of G whose removal disconnects the graph into two connected components, one of which is P. Furthermore, we say that P is a maximal dangling path if it is not a proper subgraph of some other dangling path of G. Achieving all three goals described above insures that, with non- negligible probability, there is a maximal dangling path of length Ω(log n) in Cα,ν(n) contained in region Ra.",
