"arXiv:1102.0300v4 [math.PR] 16 Mar 2012 Invertibility of symmetric random matrices Roman Vershynin∗ University of Michigan romanv@umich.edu February 1, 2011; last revised March 16, 2012 Abstract We study n × n symmetric random matrices H, possibly discrete, with iid above-diagonal entries.",
"We show that H is singular with probability at most exp(−nc), and ∥H−1∥= O(√n).",
"Furthermore, the spectrum of H is delocalized on the optimal scale o(n−1/2).",
"These results improve upon a polynomial singularity bound due to Costello, Tao and Vu, and they generalize, up to constant factors, results of Tao and Vu, and Erd¨os, Schlein and Yau.",
"Keywords: Symmetric random matrices, invertibility problem, singularity probability.",
