"To see what we mean, ﬁrst note that the move of the Bulgarian solitaire consists in applying the following two substeps to the corresponding Etienne diagram (see Figure 2): • apply the cyclic shift (from left to right) to each row of the diagram; • if after the shift there is a particle that is placed above an empty cell, then the particle falls there; this procedure is repeated until no further fall is possible.",
