"PLAGIARISM DETECTION In 1927 Charles Bird “first researched the application of statistical methods in the detection of plagiarism with multiple choice answers” (Chong, 2013).",
"In the 1960s, the first methods were developed aiming to detect plagiarism of texts with multiple choice answers, whereas the first systems for plagiarism detection of written texts were developed in the 1970s for source code, and in the 1990s for natural languages (Chong, 2013).",
"T. Vrbanec, A. Meštrović: Taxonomy of academic plagiarism methods Zbornik Veleučilišta u Rijeci, Vol.",
