"It achieves F1-score of 0.9167, Although this method did not outperform the results achieved through direct fine-tuning (F1-score of 0.9454) on the noisy dataset, it captured distinct patterns Data Model Test F1-Score Label-A Label-B deberta-v3-xsmall 0.9985 0.6382 deberta-v3-small 1.0 0.9454 deberta-v3-base 0.9989 0.6570 Noised train/val Double Finetune (deberta-v3-small) - 0.9167 Ensemble (deberta-v3-small + Double Finetune) - 0.9531 Best performing submission 1.0 0.9531 Table 4 Major system submissions and nuances within the data.",
These unique patterns proved valuable when integrating the outputs into a weighted (60:40) ensemble model for Task-B which reports the best F1-score of 0.9531.,
"By leveraging the complementary strengths of models fine-tuned on raw and noisy datasets, the ensemble model was able to outperform all our previous experiments.",
"This approach highlights the utility of combining diverse training strategies to capture a broader range of data characteristics, ultimately leading to a more robust and effective system.",
Our findings underscore the relevance of data noising as a practical tool for improving language model generalization and stability in AI generated text detection.,
