"From these four tables we can extract the following conclusions: • As expected, the listed bound values are indeed upper bounds for the variances.",
• None of the bounds is always the tightest.,
"• B3 is always the tightest bound except in one case (second row of Example 3) • In examples 3 and 4, the bounds are much less tight, while in Example 2 the bounds are very tight.",
• The weighted harmonic mean is in most cases tighter than the bounds.,
"However, we recall that it is not a bound, as we observe in Example 4.",
"Conclusions In this paper, we have proposed a multiple importance sampling estimator that combines samples simulated from diﬀerent techniques.",
"The novel estimator generalizes the bal- ance heuristic estimator, widely used Monte Carlo in the literature of signal processing, computational statistics, and computer graphics.",
