"5 Conclusions In conclusion, given an alphabet Z with a ﬁnite number of letters and with a true PMF P and an estimated PMF Q, the measure of their divergence should 9 be bounded if one interprets the divergence based on the ineﬃciency caused by using Q instead of P in coding Z.",
