(a) a wasteful binary tree (b) the most unbalanced binary tree Figure 7: Two examples of binary codes illustrated as binary trees.,
"alphabet Z = {z1,z2}.",
"Regardless what PMF is associated with Z, Z can always be encoded with a 1-bit code, e.g., codeword 0 for z1 and codeword 1 for z2, as long as neither of the two probability values in P is zero, i.e., p1 ̸= 0 and p2 ̸= 0.",
"However, if we had followed Eq.",
