"In con- trast to MambaResNetn, which operates on image intensities, MambaNetn processes gradient-domain inputs, enabling the modeling of nonlocal interactions between image gradients.",
"Specifically, the network takes V “ ∇I as the primary input, while the auxiliary branches process the gradients of the enhanced and histogram-equalized images, ∇IWB and ∇IHE.",
"In this case, the output of the MLP is directly used as the enhanced gradient representation.",
