A lot of recent research has focused on extending the classical TV model for grayscale images to vector-valued (color or multichannel) images.,
"We provide below an initial overview on vectorial total variation, which will be detailed and link to our framework in Section 3.",
"1.1 Vector Valued Total Variation Let Ω⊂RM be a bounded domain, then the scalar total variation of a locally integrable function u ∈L1 loc (Ω, R) is TV(u) := sup ξ∈Ξ Z Ω u(x) div (ξ(x)) dx  , (1) where x = (x1, .",
