Almost all empiri- cal studies in visualization involve measuring participants’ perfor- mance in visualization processes.,
"Such measured data allow us to assess the beneﬁt of visualization or potential misinterpretation, typically in terms of accuracy and response time.",
Many uncon- trolled empirical studies also collect participants’ experience and opinions qualitatively.,
The empirical studies related to the key com- ponents are those on the topics of visual abstraction and human knowledge in visualization.,
Isenberg [Ise13] presented a survey of evaluation techniques on non-photorealistic and illustrative render- ing.,
