"Consider that the designer is given a metro map designed using alphabet B, and is asked to produce a more abstract map using al- phabet A.",
"To the designer, it is a straightforward task, since there is only one option in A.",
"When a group of viewers are visualizing the ﬁnal design a1, we could give these viewers a task to guess what may be the original map designed with B.",
"If most viewers have no knowledge about the possible options b2 and b3, and almost all choose b1 as the original design, we can describe their decisions using a PMF P such that p1 = 0.998, p2 = p3 = 0.001.",
"Since P is not the same as either Qu or Qv, the viewers’ decisions diverge from the actual PMF associated with B.",
