"(4) 3.2 Nonlocal Retinex-based variational model We propose to simultaneously estimate the illu- mination, reflectance, and noise by solving the following minimization problem: min R,L,N 1 2}R ˝ L ` N ´ ˜I}2 2 ` α}∇ωR}2,1,2 ` β 2 }∇L}2,1 ` λ 2 }N}2 2 ` µ 2 }p∇R ´ ∇ˆIqˆω}2 2, (5) where α, β, λ, µ ą 0 are trade-off parameters.",
"The first term corresponds to the decomposition model but considers ˜I P RCˆM, a color corrected version of the low-light image computed following the pro- cedure described in Subsection 3.3, instead of I.",
"The α-term enforces nonlocal total variation spar- sity, which serves as a useful prior for preserving fine details and texture in the reflectance compo- nent, the β-term promotes total variation in the illumination component to reduce noise and recon- struct the main geometrical structure, while the λ-term constrains the amount of noise.",
"The µ-term is a newly proposed nonlo- cal gradient-type constraint that minimizes the nonlocal distance between the gradient of the reflectance and the gradient of ˆI P RCˆM, a pre-processed version of ˜I.",
"This pre-processing involves applying BM3D to ˜I for denoising [45], followed by gamma correction on each channel, as described in Subsection 3.6.",
"In this setting, ˆω P RMˆMˆ2 is a non-negative weight function, assumed to be the same across channels.",
"The non- local vector p∇R ´ ∇ˆIqˆω P RCˆMˆMˆ2 is defined for each channel k, each component t and at each pair of pixels i and j as ` p∇R´∇ˆIqˆω ˘ k,i,j,t “ a ˆωi,j,tpp∇Rqk,i,t´p∇ˆIqk,j,tq.",
