"Conclusion In this paper, we introduced MV-MLM, a Multi-View Vision-Language Contrastive Learning model designed for breast cancer/anomaly detection and risk prediction from mammography images.",
Our method addresses the lim- ited availability of paired mammogram-report datasets by aligning high-resolution mammograms with synthetic text reports generated from structured annotations.,
"MV-MLM outperformed existing CLIP-based, SSL, and fully super- vised methods on malignancy classification, breast mass and calcification estimation, as well as risk prediction tasks across public datasets (VinDr-Mammo and RSNA- Mammo).",
"The strong performance and generalization ca- pabilities demonstrate MV-MLM’s potential for clinical applications, especially considering the the transferability shown during linear probing.",
Future work includes extend- ing our approach to other imaging modalities and enhanc- ing interpretability for modalities with limited annotated data.,
