"Accordingly, from the above terms and the Figure 3-5 it is possible to define metrics that could reduce the bias in ""metrics"" when we have unbalance databases.",
"𝑇𝑟𝑢𝑒𝑃𝑜𝑠𝑖𝑡𝑖𝑣𝑒𝑅𝑎𝑡𝑒= 𝑇𝑟𝑢𝑒𝑃𝑜𝑠𝑖𝑡𝑖𝑣𝑒 𝐹𝑎𝑙𝑠𝑒𝑁𝑒𝑔𝑎𝑡𝑖𝑣𝑒+ 𝑇𝑟𝑢𝑒𝑃𝑜𝑠𝑖𝑡𝑖𝑣𝑒 (3.2) The equation (3.2) or Sensitivity corresponds to the fraction of positive samples that are correctly predicted as positive, with respect to the whole positive data samples.",
"𝑇𝑟𝑢𝑒𝑁𝑒𝑔𝑎𝑡𝑖𝑣𝑒𝑅𝑎𝑡𝑒= 𝑇𝑟𝑢𝑒𝑁𝑒𝑔𝑎𝑡𝑖𝑣𝑒 𝐹𝑎𝑙𝑠𝑒𝑃𝑜𝑠𝑖𝑡𝑖𝑣𝑒+ 𝑇𝑟𝑢𝑒𝑁𝑒𝑔𝑎𝑡𝑖𝑣𝑒 (3.3) The equation (3.3) or Specificity corresponds to the fraction of negative samples that are correctly predicted as negative, with respect to the whole negative data samples.",
