2.2 Candidate Selection Previous work by [9] was employed to detect suspicious mass candidates.,
1) shows sample MLO view DM images of left and right breast.,
Likelihood of a pixel to be part of a mass was computed using local lines and distribution of gradient orientation features.,
"Then, a global threshold was applied to the likelihood image to generate regions that are considered as suspicious.",
The red and green points correspond to suspected candidate center locations of mass.,
