"Moreover, TabNet mistakes raised markers for vertical patches in almost a third of the examples, raised crosswalks for speed bumps in a fourth of the examples, and speed bumps for raised crosswalks in a fifth of the examples.",
"At the same time, TabNet is 85.19% accurate when predicting vertical patches, only mistaking them for raised crosswalks and speed bumps in 3.70% of the time, and for raised markers in 7.41% of the time.",
