"3 Historical Evolution of Tabular Deep Learning 3.1 Classical Approaches Before the emergence of deep learning, traditional machine learning models like Support Vector Machines (SVMs), linear and logistic regression, and tree-based methods have long been the preferred choice for tabular data analysis [48].",
These classical approaches were well-suited for small-scale tabular datasets but limited to classification and regression tasks.,
"These models were not only highly interpretable, allowing users to understand and explain predictions, but they also handled both numerical and categorical data well.",
"They were ideally suited for small to medium- sized datasets, as they required less computational power and were quick to train.",
